    {
      "id": "znw6fl6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.1 Training vs Development vs Education"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Training focuses on immediate job-specific skills, Education builds conceptual understanding, and Development prepares individuals for future career growth.",
        "Training Need Analysis (TNA) identifies performance gaps across Organizational, Task, and Individual levels before designing programs.",
        "Training methods are categorized into On-the-Job (OJT) and Off-the-Job techniques depending on practical vs classroom context.",
        "Kirkpatrick's Four-Level Model provides a structured framework to evaluate training effectiveness from immediate reaction to overall business results.",
        "Management Development Programmes (MDP) focus on enhancing conceptual, managerial, and executive skills for prospective business leaders."
      ],
      "id": "jpra0ld"
    },
